    {
      "id": "s2018-e3-q06",
      "number": 6,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "Which of the following represents the power series for the product of the two convergent power series\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{1 - 2x} = 1 + 2x + 4x^2 + 8x^3 + \\cdots\n$$\n\n$$\n\\ln(1 + x) = x - \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + \\frac{1}{3}x^3 - \\frac{1}{4}x^4 + \\cdots\n$$",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$1 + 2x^2 - x^4 + \\cdots$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$x - x^2 + 2x^3 + \\cdots$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$x + \\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \\frac{10}{3}x^3 + \\cdots$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$x - x^3 + \\frac{4}{3}x^5 + \\cdots$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$1 + x + 3x^2 + 5x^3 + \\cdots$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "C",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L32"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 5,
      "solution": "The official key accepted every choice for this question.\n\nMultiply the two series and collect terms up to $x^3$. The product has no constant term, since $\\ln(1 + x)$ has none.\n\n$$\n(1 + 2x + 4x^2 + \\cdots)\\left(x - \\frac{1}{2}x^2 + \\frac{1}{3}x^3 - \\cdots\\right)\n$$\n\n- $x$: $1 \\cdot x = x$\n- $x^2$: $1 \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) + 2 \\cdot 1 = \\frac{3}{2}$\n- $x^3$: $1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} + 2 \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) + 4 \\cdot 1 = \\frac{10}{3}$\n\nSo the product is $x + \\frac{3}{2}x^2 + \\frac{10}{3}x^3 + \\cdots$, which is choice C.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
